      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          The best protein powder for seniors delivers 25 to 30 g of high-quality protein per serving, little or no sugar, and is easy enough to mix that it actually gets used. For most older adults that means a whey-based powder or a ready-to-drink milk protein shake. Our top pick is Ensure Max Protein, a ready-to-drink shake with about 30 g of protein and about 1 g of sugar per bottle, per the label. The reason it matters is well documented: muscle loss accelerates with age, older muscle responds less to small doses of protein, and expert groups now recommend that healthy adults over 65 eat more protein than the standard adult RDA. The one important exception is kidney disease, covered below.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="quick-comparison" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. The Quick Answer: Our Picks Compared
          </h2>

          <p>
            Here is the whole field at a glance. Ready-to-drink shakes are listed alongside powders because, for many older adults, the best protein supplement is the one that needs no scoop, shaker or blender. Price tier compares cost per serving at typical retail prices, not the price of a tub or case.
          </p>

